# Trader cron schedule (SPEC §9), run by supercronic in the container (P4-T10).
# Times are US Eastern wall-clock times: CRON_TZ makes supercronic read them in America/New_York, so they
# follow the DST changes. Every job is idempotent and does nothing on a holiday (it prints
# "not a trading session"). The 12:55 flatten is the backup for early-close days (13:00 close); on a normal
# day it is too early and does nothing. The 12:32 and 15:32 `event --due` lines back up the overlay decision
# (close - 30 min: 12:30 on early-close days, 15:30 otherwise); `--due` fires only events that are due and
# not yet settled, so on a normal day the 12:32 run finds nothing new. The 12:58 and 15:58 flatten lines are a
# second backup (P3-REVIEW): if the worker is down and the first backup fails, a retry still runs before the
# close (the flatten is a safety event, so its failures never settle it). The Saturday 09:00 `trader weekly`
# line (P5-T17) reports the Monday-Friday week just ended, keyed by that week's last session; it runs although
# Saturday is not a session and does nothing for a week without one. Retries of the day-level jobs happen
# in-process (SPEC section 9), so there are no retry lines here. The two `soak-report --notify` lines (P6-T2)
# send one read-only soak/ops line per session: weekdays 18:05 after the post-close and its retries, and
# Saturday 10:30 after the weekly report, settling the week's last session (`--final`). QUOTEBAR: the 09:47
# `openbar-check` compares the 9:35 opening bars built from live quotes with the official 09:30-09:35 candles,
# which Stephen's market-data package publishes ~10 minutes late; it retries in-process until 10:30.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York
0 2 * * *      trader token-refresh
0 20 * * 0-4   trader nightly
0 8 * * 1-5    trader premarket
20 9 * * 1-5   trader preopen
36 9 * * 1-5   trader event orb_open
47 9 * * 1-5   trader openbar-check
30 11 * * 1-5  trader checkin --at 11:30
32 12 * * 1-5  trader event --due
55 12 * * 1-5  trader event flatten
58 12 * * 1-5  trader event flatten
30 13 * * 1-5  trader checkin --at 13:30
32 15 * * 1-5  trader event --due
55 15 * * 1-5  trader event flatten
58 15 * * 1-5  trader event flatten
15 16 * * 1-5  trader postclose
0 9 * * 6      trader weekly
5 18 * * 1-5   trader soak-report --notify
30 10 * * 6    trader soak-report --notify --final
